(findings . ((decision-honesty . "the evidence record, the W1 decision block it cites, and the ci.yml hold notice all say the same thing: hold, because the security gate is unevaluable from zero paired samples; nothing is dressed up as timing evidence")
             (targets . "the gate text (security p50 <= 240 s, semantics unchanged, no reliability regression versus paired batch) is quoted from the roadmap v1.00.25 §6 W4 text; no revision, no reinterpretation, and the W1 rule that a missed gate never becomes a revised target is honored by recording hold")
             (evidence-provenance . "paired-samples 0 and the fast/batch/fifo baseline numbers (20 samples, p50 228.5815 s, p95 235.9965 s) match the W1 evidence record and artifacts/ci-baseline/v1.00.25-c1/decision.md; the record explicitly labels the fast baseline as not a security-lane baseline")
             (scheduler-neutrality . "the contract pins in tests/test-run-tests-profiles.rkt (scheduler-token absence in the security job block, byte-verbatim --suite security run command, batch-env lever still forcing batch, repository-variable guard across all of ci.yml) make any silent activation a deliberate pin break; with nothing activated, permission/isolation/sandbox semantics are unchanged by construction")
             (cli-default-untouched . "scripts/run-tests.rkt has no scheduler default change in this wave; only a workflow comment and test pins changed")
             (next-lever-named . "the record names the concrete next lever: close the C1 security/queue/fifo shadow leg with real scheduled-run evidence and re-run the reviewed gate decision")))
(residual-risks . "while the C1 security shadow leg has zero recorded attempts, the security lane's queue timing characteristics remain unknown; any future promote must be decided on real paired samples, and the W4 guard pins must be relaxed deliberately, never silently")
